  "articleBody": "Ever open your closet and feel like you're rummaging in the dark, even with a light on? It's a common issue! Often, it comes down to a few things. Sometimes, we just don't have enough light fixtures for the size of the space, or the bulbs aren't bright enough. Another big culprit is fixture placement; if your light is right in the middle of the ceiling, your clothes on the rod can create shadows, making it tough to see what's on the shelves below. People also sometimes use fixtures that aren't actually designed to spread light effectively in a closet, leading to those dark corners. Plus, those old bare bulbs? Not only are they often dim, but they're usually a no-go for safety in closets these days. Getting the right lumen output and thinking about how light will actually hit your clothes and shelves can make a huge difference. If you're struggling to light up your closet effectively, it might be time for an upgrade. HH Remodeling LLC can help you figure out a brighter solution.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}